<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Geolsa Biu</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 697</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a> · Also known as Qishi Biyu</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Geolsa Biu was a chief of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mohe">Mohe people</a> who led his followers east from the Yingzhou region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tang-dynasty">Tang China</a> after the Khitan revolt of 696, together with the Goguryeo leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dae-jung-sang">Dae Jung-sang</a>. He refused a Tang offer of a title and was killed in battle with a pursuing Tang army. His people then joined <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dae-joyeong">Dae Joyeong</a>, who went on to found Balhae.</p></div>
